#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="tests/**, src/**"

TEST_COMMAND:
- make test (runs unit tests on host via SDCC-portable C code)
- Emulator-based runtime testing: load build/<rom>.gb in BGB or SameBoy
- SameBoy supports headless mode + Lua scripting for automated checks: sameboy --headless --script tests/scenarios/<name>.lua
- BGB has accurate hardware emulation but no headless mode — use for manual regression

TEST_CONVENTIONS:
- Pure-logic functions (no Game Boy hardware deps) → unit-test on host using a small wrapper that stubs GBDK headers
- Hardware-dependent code → emulator scenario tests
- Scenario naming: tests/scenarios/<feature>.lua mirrors src/<feature>.c
- Cycle-budget tests: assert frame-time stays under VBlank window (one frame = 70224 cycles at DMG speed)
- ROM-size budget tests: fail the build if compiled ROM exceeds the target cartridge size

COVERAGE_REQUIREMENTS:
- (fill in — coverage tools for SDCC are limited; track manually for now)

FORBIDDEN_IN_TESTS:
- No emulator timing assumptions without a SameBoy/BGB version pin
- No save-state shortcuts that bypass actual RAM/persistence code paths (you'll miss the bugs that matter)
- No skipping serial-link tests if the project uses link cable — tested only on emulator with link-cable simulation
